course: dictionary
lesson: 15636
title: Words that can be ended
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Terminable is an adjective. It means able to be ended or stopped, and you will mostly find it in formal writing about contracts and agreements. «The phone contract is terminable with one month's notice.» This means the contract can be ended, but only after one month's warning.
explain: Look at the word parts. Term means an end or a fixed limit, and -able means can be. So terminable means can be ended. «The club membership is terminable at any time.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Something that can be ended. Then swap your meaning in and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Terminable can also describe something with a limited time that will come to an end. «The loan is terminable after five years» tells you the loan finishes when five years are up. Do not mix it up with terrible or terminal. They look similar but mean different things.
fact: Terminable means able to be ended or stopped.
fact: «Terminable» is mostly found in formal and legal writing, especially about contracts and agreements.
fact: Two phrases you may see are «terminable at will», meaning it can be ended at any time, and «terminable on notice», meaning it can be ended once one side gives warning.
fact: Term means an end or limit, and -able means can be, so the word's parts give you its meaning.
exercise: «The rental agreement is terminable with one month's notice.» What does terminable mean here? | Written in French | Never able to change | Very long and difficult | *Able to be ended
exercise: Ben says terminable means the same as terrible. What is the right meaning? | Very bad or awful | Bad at sport | *Able to be ended or stopped | Limited to one day only
exercise: «The trial period was terminable after 30 days.» Which phrase tells you the trial will come to an end? | trial period | days | *terminable after 30 days | was
test: «The club membership is terminable.» What does this tell you? | It has already been lost | *It can be ended | It cannot be changed | It is free forever
test: Which sentence uses terminable correctly? | «The bus is terminable at my desk.» | *«The agreement is terminable on one month's notice.» | «The sky is terminable at night.» | «My dog is terminable and very happy.»
exam: Which phrase from a contract means it can be ended at any time? | unlimited | perpetual | *terminable at will | hereditary
